{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/957252-interest-in-a-v20-play-by-post-game","id":957252,"title":"Interest in a V20 play by post game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-24T16:18:12-07:00","id":957252,"title":"Interest in a V20 play by post game?","content":"I am looking at doing a play by post V20 game. I would want people who can post at least once every couple days, daily being better. The general idea is that several of the major Giovanni families are planning to do the Giovanni, as the Giovanni did to the Cappadocians. Player characters would not know this initially. Non-single blooded members of clan Giovanni are ideal, but if you can sell me on why a member of another clan would be trusted enough to be involved I will allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T17:57:01-07:00","id":957293,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind a Giovanni game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:35:59-07:00","id":957975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/957252-interest-in-a-v20-play-by-post-game?p=957293#post957293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't mind a Giovanni game.</div> </div> </div> </div>cool, but I need at least 3 people to go ahead with things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:25:08-07:00","id":958343,"title":"","content":"Hey, if you don't mind playing with a person that is not a walking encyclopedia of oWoD lore (but still knows enough to get by) then count me in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:39:43-07:00","id":958353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woland</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/957252-interest-in-a-v20-play-by-post-game?p=958343#post958343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, if you don't mind playing with a person that is not a walking encyclopedia of oWoD lore (but still knows enough to get by) then count me in.</div> </div> </div> </div>My knowledge of world of darkness is hardly perfect so that shouldn't be an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:54:43-07:00","id":958434,"title":"","content":"An all one (or mostly one clan) would be an interesting change of pace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T18:49:08-07:00","id":958549,"title":"","content":"That gives us 3. For character creation as I said in the OP non-single blooded giovanni (so members of clan Giovanni that are part of one of the families that aren't Giovanni) are probably the best characters to play, but if you can sell me on why the elders of those families would trust non-family to be involved in the coup then other clans are fine as well. The plan is for you to start in the UK, but you will probably travel across Europe and North America as part of the campaign. Use the basic rules from V20 for making your character, if you are wanting to use an option from another V20 book let me know and what source it is from, I don't always remember what non-main rulebook stuff is in what book.<br /> <br /> For those of you that want to refresh your memories about the major families of the Giovanni clan, lore of the clans and the old giovanni clanbooks are the best sources.<br /> <br /> I can have up to 5 people, so there is still space for two more if others are interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:54:50-07:00","id":958852,"title":"","content":"I'd like to make a Milliner, since there's still room. I'll come up with something for approval.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T13:09:20-07:00","id":958860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/957252-interest-in-a-v20-play-by-post-game?p=958852#post958852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to make a Milliner, since there's still room. I'll come up with something for approval.</div> </div> </div> </div>cool, looking forward to seeing your character<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:47:41-07:00","id":958925,"title":"","content":"It seems that you can't attach text files to private messages, so l'll just post my character here. If something doesn't add up please tell me; I have lowered my Generation through the use of Background points but if you don't allow it then I can come up with something different.<br /> <br /> Oh hell, now it tells me that my .pdf file is &quot;invalid data&quot;. Can anyone more forum-savvy offer a solution?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I am absolutely done with figuring out how to add attachements to a post, so here are Google Drive links to the files.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2ex3DicLU7ga2t1dzd5bWFXQ00/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2e...ew?usp=sharing</a> - character background<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2ex3DicLU7gYzFXVWxHc3pocjQ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2e...ew?usp=sharing</a> - character sheet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","user":"Woland","date":". 09-01-2016, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:55:46-07:00","id":958931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woland</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/957252-interest-in-a-v20-play-by-post-game?p=958925#post958925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems that you can't attach text files to private messages, so l'll just post my character here. If something doesn't add up please tell me; I have lowered my Generation through the use of Background points but if you don't allow it then I can come up with something different.<br /> <br /> Oh hell, now it tells me that my .pdf file is &quot;invalid data&quot;. Can anyone more forum-savvy offer a solution?</div> </div> </div> </div>Screenshot the page? crop the stuff not in the PDF then upload the picture file?<br /> <br /> Also it makes sense to me that some or many of the kindred chosen to fill key roles in this plan would be of relatively low generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","user":"Browman","date":". 08-27-2016, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T03:08:36-07:00","id":959159,"title":"","content":"So, there's room for a fifth, it seems? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Never played a Giovani, but always loved necromancy. If you give me a day you'll have my character ready.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T05:35:09-07:00","id":959183,"title":"","content":"Sounds good Thorbes.<br /> <br /> Woland I have 1 question, your character is a highly intelligent, almost 200 year old 8th gen. Why does he only have the skills and disciplines of a neonate? Neonates are normally 10-20 years embraced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T06:42:53-07:00","id":959206,"title":"","content":"Well, as for the Disciplines I just figured that the guy was so focused on discerning the necromantic secrets that he cared little for Dominating others or punching through walls with Potence. Necromancy rituals are closely guarded, however, especially from someone who technically is not &quot;family&quot; (his last name is not Pisanob) - hence so little dots. You're probably right that the lack of Skill dots cannot be so easily explained, except maybe for the fact that he has spent practically his entire existence reading books and doing field research on his favorite subjects, and after a few decades it is just hard to find enough information that can actually amount to another dot.<br /> <br /> This is an overall valid concern and if you prefer I can make my character younger by around a century. Just say the word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:42:00-07:00","id":959241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woland</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/957252-interest-in-a-v20-play-by-post-game?p=959206#post959206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as for the Disciplines I just figured that the guy was so focused on discerning the necromantic secrets that he cared little for Dominating others or punching through walls with Potence. Necromancy rituals are closely guarded, however, especially from someone who technically is not &amp;quot;family&amp;quot; (his last name is not Pisanob) - hence so little dots. You're probably right that the lack of Skill dots cannot be so easily explained, except maybe for the fact that he has spent practically his entire existence reading books and doing field research on his favorite subjects, and after a few decades it is just hard to find enough information that can actually amount to another dot.<br /> <br /> This is an overall valid concern and if you prefer I can make my character younger by around a century. Just say the word.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps he spent a few decades in torpor for some reason? He could be that old but have a reason for lower skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T08:05:03-07:00","id":959251,"title":"","content":"Will being staked by hunters for 80 years suffice? Let's say there was an assault on one of the more remote Pisanob safehouses around the 1920s, while the guy was without his sire. He got stabbed at the beginning, which was the entire reason he is still in one piece - the attackers were so busy destroying the inhabitants and the lore within that they simply overlooked him. After these decades the stake in his heart shifted just enough for him to awake and forcing him to travel all the way to the main temple, where he was not only seriously weakend but also mistrusted (after all this time, who can say he is not a sleeper agent or worse?) - which impaired his ability to learn Disciplines/skills and made him focus on regaining trust. Eventually the family concluded that he can be sent to the UK, because if he is a traitor then he can do limited harm half a world away (not to mention he can be destroyed, sparing Pisanob the effort) and if he isn't and actually performs well the Necromancers can enjoy a low-cost victory. A win-win either way.<br /> <br /> If you like it I will make appropriate changes in the background document shortly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T08:14:10-07:00","id":959255,"title":"","content":"[here was a double post. Again. It appears that you can't delete your own posts, which is a shame]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","user":"Woland","date":". 08-28-2016, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T08:46:32-07:00","id":959275,"title":"","content":"Sounds good to me, Mexico had a few bad (like 7+ on the Richter scale) earthquakes between 1995 and 2003. That could explain why the stake shifted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T10: